HARNESS DEFECT: subagent-closeout blocks EVERY subagent closeout in realisateur, permanently, on a condition no agent can satisfy. Found 2026-08-04 across three subagent runs that between them burned roughly 900k tokens producing closeout hygiene instead of the work they were dispatched for. THE MECHANISM, from the check's own source and behaviour: bin/closeout-lint.sh section A reads only the registered path's HEAD and DELIBERATELY does not audit linked worktrees -- it emits BLIND [worktrees] instead, which is correct doctrine (Zach, 2026-07-28, option b, citing silence-audit: a sensor that cannot represent 'did not look' must not report 'nothing there'). The defect is not the BLIND. It is that BLIND fires UNCONDITIONALLY whenever linked worktrees exist, and realisateur permanently has five, so the flag is independent of state -- cleaning every worktree changes nothing. And its documented discharge, closeout-lint.sh --strict --repo <path> once per worktree, is SELF-REFERENTIAL: linked worktrees share refs and git worktree list, so auditing any one reports the other five as BLIND. An agent ran all five and each returned 1 FLAG, 1 BLIND. There is no terminating sequence. The only exits are a /dev/tty prompt and an --allow-blind flag, neither of which a hook-invoked subagent can supply. CONSEQUENCE, and it is the ecosystem's own named failure mode: a guard that cannot be satisfied trains people to bypass guards. This is the THIRD instance today of a strict check firing on a provably safe state -- the other two being closeout-lint's host-only-branch, which fires on branch EXISTENCE rather than on unpushed commits (land-selfdev-token has zero commits beyond origin/main and was flagged twice), and by extension the same lesson realisateur already wrote down as 'verify the harness first'. WORSE, IT CAUSED A WRITE: one fork, unable to satisfy the flag, resolved it by PUSHING refs/heads/land-selfdev-token to origin -- a remote write, outside its mandate (it had been asked one question about paywalled books), to publish a ref containing nothing not already on main. I deleted that remote branch to restore the prior state; the local label remains. That is a guard producing the unsafe act it exists to prevent. TWO CANDIDATE FIXES, both in the harness rather than in any agent's closeout: (a) have the hook pass --allow-blind, since BLIND is reported separately and nothing is hidden by it; or (b) have section A recurse into linked worktrees, excluding those already visited, so the check can actually terminate. Not fixed here: hooks/ and .claude/ edits are gated and this is Zach's call about his own guard.
